================================================================================
RK4 INTERPOLATION CODE ANALYSIS
================================================================================

  The GPU RK4 code (rk4_fully_fused_timedep.py) has these potential issues:

  1. NEGATIVE INDEX ACCESS (connectivity[-1]):
     When elem_id = -1 (search failed), the interpolation function reads
     connectivity[-1] (Python wraps to LAST element). JAX jnp.where masks the
     output to zero, but the computation itself runs on wrong data.
     → This is safe for VELOCITY (masked to zero), but could cause issues in
       the SEARCH (L0 check of connectivity[-1] element).

  2. RK4 SUB-STEP SEARCH CHAIN:
     If stage k1 search fails (elem_k1 = -1), vel_k1 = zero, pos_k1 = pos.
     Stage k2 then searches from elem_k1 = -1 as cached element.
     L0 check: connectivity[-1] → last element → likely NOT containing pos.
     L1 search: start from -1 → masked out (should_search = False) → returns -1.
     L2 search: full octree search → should find the correct element.
     → If L2 search ALSO fails: ALL subsequent stages get zero velocity,
       and pos_final = pos (no movement). elem_final search may then also fail
       → particle permanently lost with elem_id = -1.

  3. BARYCENTRIC COORD ACCUMULATION:
     If particle is at edge/vertex of element, barycentric coords can have
     slight numerical errors. Velocity is computed correctly, but the position
     update pos_k1 = pos + 0.5*dt*vel_k1 may push the particle slightly
     outside the element. If the new position is in a registration gap
     (not covered by 3×3×3 neighborhood), the search fails.
     → This is the most likely cause of tetrahedral-shaped voids.

  4. SINGLE VELOCITY FIELD PER RK4 STEP:
     All 4 stages (k1..k4) use the SAME velocity_field[vel_idx], even though
     stages k2/k3 evaluate at t+dt/2 and k4 at t+dt. For time-dependent flows,
     this means the time interpolation is missing. If the real code uses
     different timesteps for different stages, this could cause different
     trajectories than FEMUSS.


